Title: [Perf][GLM-5.3] Fuse the KDA decode glue kernels into two launches

Branch: pr-glm5next-kda-decode-glue (base 1Cat main 022349e47), one commit (squash of our fork commits b817aa185 and 381a4eac7; the second fixed the first before it was ever sent)
Status: DRAFT, not sent. Items marked RECHECK must be re-measured on this branch before sending. The new CUDA test has not been run on a GPU in this tree yet.

----- Text -----

Problem: In decode and speculative-verify steps the GLM-5.3 KDA layer (Glm5NextLinearAttention) launches 15 tiny kernels around the recurrent kernel: four .contiguous() copies of q, k, v and beta that fused_recurrent_kda makes of the strided conv output and beta, before it, and, after it, the eager FusedRMSNormGated.forward_native chain of 11 kernels for the fp32 output norm. At 1 to 8 rows each of them costs a launch and no real work, in every one of the 34 KDA layers of every step.

Change:
- New vllm/model_executor/layers/fla/ops/sm70/kda_glue.py with two Triton kernels. kda_pack_recurrent_inputs packs q, k, v (1, T, H, D) and beta (1, T, H) into contiguous buffers in one launch (a pure copy). kda_gated_rmsnorm replaces the eager chain in one launch and follows torch's fp32 operation order: x*x stored before summing (enable_fp_fusion=False, no FMA contraction), four sequential values per lane then torch's halving tree over 32 lanes (lane i with lane i + 16, 8, 4, 2, 1), the exact mean scale 1/128, IEEE expf and division for the sigmoid, one rounding cast. The output is therefore bit-identical to forward_native.
- vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/kda.py: the fp32 output norm branch calls kda_gated_rmsnorm; the non-fp32 branch keeps the CustomOp dispatch of #1165. A new Glm5NextLinearAttention._recurrent_inputs packs q, k, v and beta for the spec and non-spec recurrent calls when more than one row is present (for a single row the views are already contiguous and are used as before). The q|k|v split of the plain-decode path that is no longer needed is removed.
- Prefill, the chunked kernel and the PP/graph structure are untouched.

Evidence:
- Bit-identity: tests/models/glm5next/test_kda_glue.py (CUDA only) asserts torch.equal against forward_native for 1, 5, 6 and 8 rows and input scales 1, 1000 and 1e-3, and of the packed tensors against .contiguous(). Our run on a V100 (fork, same kernel file): all 12 norm cases and 4 pack cases torch.equal. RECHECK: run this file on this branch on V100 and on Quadro RTX 8000.
- Launches: 15 -> 2 per KDA layer in a decode or verify step.
- Time in a CUDA graph at 8 rows, per KDA layer: 42.9 us less on V100 and 37.5 us less on Quadro RTX 8000, bit-identical (RECHECK: re-run the micro-benchmark on this branch).
- End to end: in our fork a bundle of this change, the router GEMM fix, the sort-based MoE routing kernel (separate PRs) and a merge of 1Cat main measured GLM-5.3-Flash decode (short prompts, 192 tokens, greedy) 41.99 -> 44.50 and 44.41 tok/s on PP5 over 3x V100 + 2x Quadro RTX 8000. That figure belongs to the bundle, not to this change alone. RECHECK: A/B of this change alone on this branch.

Tests (on main 022349e47 plus this commit; CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES empty, our wrapper around python -m pytest, one process per file):
- tests/models/glm5next/test_kda_glue.py: 16 skipped (needs CUDA); to be run on a GPU before sending (RECHECK).
- Other files under tests/models/glm5next: test_kda_norm_dispatch.py 2 passed 2 skipped; test_mtp_config.py 4 passed; test_sm70_kda.py 17 passed 25 skipped; test_sm70_sparse.py 4 passed 6 skipped; test_vision_budget.py 6 passed; test_pp.py 6 passed 2 failed (AttributeError: 'Glm5NextModel' object has no attribute '_pp_aux_dump' in test_glm53_materialized_mhc_state_crosses_pp_boundary and test_glm53_dflash_aux_hidden_states_cross_pp_boundary; the same two fail on unmodified main 022349e47). The skipped tests need CUDA and are to be run on a GPU before sending (RECHECK).
- tests/kernels/core/test_fused_rms_norm_gated.py (the eager norm this must equal; untouched): 25 failed on the CPU with RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available, identically on unmodified main (the file has no CUDA skip marker). RECHECK: to be run on a GPU.
- pre-commit run --files on the three changed files and the manual-stage mypy hook (mypy-3.10): all hooks pass.

Duplicate check: gh pr list --state all searches "KDA glue", "kda gated rmsnorm", "kda_gated_rmsnorm", "kda_glue", "glm5next decode", "KDA decode", "fused_recurrent_kda", "FusedRMSNormGated" and "GLM-5.3 decode". The merged #1165 (dispatch of the fp32 KDA output norm through its CustomOp owner) and #392/#396 (GLM KDA decode GEMV) are the earlier work on this path; none fuses the packing or replaces forward_native for the fp32 branch. Open PRs #1260, #1286, #1348 and #1549 touch vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/kda.py (prefill warmup, chunk kernel binding) and contain the unchanged o_norm and .contiguous() calls; a rebase of them onto this change may need a textual merge in kda.py.

AI assistance (Claude) was used; the change was reviewed and tested by the submitter.
